cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use binary101 in your work, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "binary101"
abstract: >-
  binary101 is a browser-based binary file analysis and inspection tool. It
  identifies and decodes a wide range of executable, archive, image, media, and
  other file formats, presenting parsed structures, offsets, decoded values,
  explanations, statistics, and previews. Executable analysis covers PE/COFF, ELF,
  and Mach-O structures, with additional support for debug and runtime metadata,
  signatures, resources, and embedded content where applicable. For PE and ELF
  files, it provides control-flow-guided x86/x86-64 and AArch64 instruction-set
  analysis. All processing is performed locally in the browser without uploading
  files.
authors:
  - family-names: "Gladskikh"
    given-names: "Sergei"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-0586-8200"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Gladskih/binary101"
url: "https://gladskih.github.io/binary101/"
license: "MIT"
keywords:
  - "binary analysis"
  - "file format analysis"
  - "executable analysis"
  - "PE"
  - "ELF"
  - "Mach-O"
  - "disassembly"
  - "instruction set analysis"
  - "x86-64"
  - "AArch64"
  - "reverse engineering"
  - "digital forensics"
  - "static analysis"
